  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001, RNA-only/singleprofile/pca_n2000) yielded ~48.5% accuracy, giving a weak baseline with high uncertainty about which design axes matter most. The single most consequential question is whether the image modality carries any discriminative signal for this task. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image modality with a standard encoder and the same single-profile structure as config_001, making it a clean one-variable comparison. If image-only accuracy is substantially different from the RNA baseline, it tells me whether multimodal fusion is worth investing the remaining 8 experiments in, or whether I should focus on RNA encoder/profile improvements. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the tight budget."
}

